    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0519" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.00/252.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santa Elena, Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1912-02-13T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1912-02-02T00:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">Not
                                dated</hi></date><hi rendition="#small-caps">; received February 13,
                            1912</hi>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Request <hi rendition="#italic">Maryland</hi> be held Santa Elena until my
                    arrival Washington, but no objection to temporary trip Panama for supplies
                    provided <hi rendition="#italic">Yorktown</hi> remains Ecuadorian waters during
                    absence <hi rendition="#italic">Maryland</hi>. Strongly urge and recommend
                    Captain Cordier, who is in touch with political situation, remain with
                    warship.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Young.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
